From: ProjectM TV contributors
Subject: [SURGICAL PROPOSAL] Bound positive remainder using integer input guards

I04 only: memcpy input representations, then use integer magnitude/sign
checks for finite, cast and original32-bit domains. No floating input
comparison, fabs or arithmetic precedes validated integer casts.
Preserve widened signed results, argument order/aliases, zero divisors
and signed minimum divided by negative-one protection.

No evaluator CMake/compiler policy change or I03 finite recovery. Existing
div/div_op/pow/pow_op/invsqrt bodies and outside NaN policy remain baseline.
Historical Apple I04-bit64/64 and NDK guards justify new qualification,
not acceptance of this revised integer-range form. Require exact Apple/
NDK fast-math IR and full76cases/20baseline-policy comparison. Supported
IEEE byte layout is explicit; MSVC/unverified platforms remain unqualified.
Root numbers/applies after proof; old alternatives/results remain frozen.

